<pardef id='7' leftmargin='1.2618in' rightmargin='93%' firstlineleftmargin='0.8118in'/>
<par def='7'><run><font style='bold' name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true'
 familyid='20'/>View</run><run><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true'
 familyid='20'/> - </run>Views are lists of documents in a Notes database. Depending on how they're designed, views can select, sort, or categorize documents in different ways. Views can also show many types of information about the documents listed in them, such as author's name or date of creation.</par>
<pardef id='8' leftmargin='0.8118in' rightmargin='93%' firstlineleftmargin='1.2618in'/>
<par def='8'>A view may show all documents in a database, or only a selection of documents.</par>
<par def='8'>Below is an example of a view used in this database.</par>
<pardef id='9' leftmargin='0.8118in' rightmargin='93%'/>
<par def='9'><run><font name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/></run></par>
